comments[17]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T20:01:13.027Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: existing computeSchedule/computeSlack and closed pm-gantt-chart-ao93 detect infeasible deadlines but do not propose repairs. Pinned core SDK lifecycle/plan exposes steps, decisions, validation and materialization, with no schedule repair solver; pm-graph README and src/index.ts expose registry-aware traversal/impact, not capacity/scope schedule search. Related pm-rl and pm-rlm README searches show no deadline repair solver. This package owns schedule-specific planning; selected changes can be recorded later through core plan. Tracker reconciliation PR #163 items are excluded. Design: exhaustive increasing-cardinality search over explicit per-item capacity offers and dependency-complete deferrals, with typed budget refusals and no tracker writes."
  "2026-10-21T20:03:18.757Z",codex-agent,"Implementation adds proposeDeadlineRepairs and gantt repair. Search certifies minimum move cardinality over explicit offers, excludes forbidden ids, rejects dangling ordering prerequisites and cycles, and refuses budget exhaustion. Local typecheck/lint/docstring/duplication completed after correcting a lint-only loop condition. Installation required npm_config_userconfig=/dev/null to bypass a user-level allow-scripts value; package pins are unchanged. Targeted regressions cover independent feasibility, no-git CLI execution without git on PATH, typed failures, immutable source bytes and capacity/scope tradeoffs."
  "2026-10-21T20:07:54.608Z",codex-agent,"Current host CLI 2026.10.21 plan --help confirms the same storage-oriented boundary; no deadline-repair command exists there. Targeted linked run passed 89/89 tests (25 new repair tests plus existing scheduler and activation tests), including real no-git installed JSON/TOON execution and durable-byte preservation. Behavioral revert proof: only the capacity application inside proposeDeadlineRepairs was temporarily replaced by returning the unchanged item; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"capacity on a prerequisite\" test/deadline-repair.test.ts failed 0/1 with no_allowed_repair instead of the expected feasible proposal. Source restored immediately. New coverage inspection identified two remaining branch arms; added focused budget and tie-ranking cases for CI. No tracker-reconciliation items were written."
  "2026-10-21T20:08:50.962Z",codex-agent,"Public read-only non-git validation at origin/main 80717afb81f1: certified 107 items, 16 active, 0 ordering edges; 1 explicitly offered expired-item deferral yielded a minimum 1-move repair, 15 retained items, 120 deferred minutes, 0 added daily capacity, completion 2026-10-25. Compact result 384 bytes; one compute-only sample 4.59 ms. Independent scheduling/slack recomputation passed; forbidding the offer returned no_allowed_repair. Durable SHA-256 snapshots were identical. Evidence: docs/deadline-repair-validation.md. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero duplication passed; 2 focused budget/tie tests passed after the earlier 89-test linked run. Full npm/Bun gates are reserved for CI as requested. Local strict health retains inherited extension version/provenance/stale-item warnings and installation fence drift; no unrelated tracker or merge work was performed."
  "2026-10-21T20:11:41.511Z",codex-agent,"PR #164 is open at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/pull/164; initial commit 674f037. Final review found that comparing formatted date strings could misclassify a schedule crossing year 9999. Replaced horizon/finish comparisons with Date comparisons while preserving inclusive timestamp-day semantics, and added an overflow/timestamp regression. Waiting for CI npm and Bun release gates before handoff; no merge or release will be performed."
  "2026-10-21T20:16:55.340Z",codex-agent,"Verified code head 7626b5209aa34cf0116e26a4301e51868bf480d7: CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/actions/runs/39668236004 passed both Node 22.18.0 and Node 26 jobs. Node 26 npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 281/281 tests, 0 failures/skips/cancellations, 100.00% lines/branches/functions across 3 runtime source files, 0% duplication and 0 production audit vulnerabilities. Packed npm/current, Bun/current and npm/minimum-host acceptance passed. Node 22 coverage also passed 281/281 at 100.00/100.00/100.00. Local npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run docstring, npm run duplication, changelog generation/check and focused regressions passed. Automated reviews remain unavailable: Greptile trial ended, Sourcery quota exhausted, CodeRabbit skipped; these are missing review evidence, not approvals. Public-copy metrics and behavioral revert proof remain in docs/deadline-repair-validation.md. No core PM CLI/SDK defect was encountered; npm installation needed a clean userconfig. Ready for orchestrator review; leave item open and do not merge/release."
  "2026-10-21T21:46:07.838Z",codex-agent,"PR #164 review round: collected all review threads and every comment (no pagination gaps); one unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6u9Nrl is valid. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff or nitpick findings. Remote head was pulled; origin/main is already an ancestor. Self-review found the same just-in-time back-anchoring defect for prerequisites with deadlines inside the horizon too. Repair feasibility now uses earliest forward scheduling and unchanged real deadlines in the backward pass; chart placement stays unchanged. Added canonical/legacy/timestamp, prerequisite/dependent, capacity-repair and earlier-deadline regressions. Initial npm ci hit host EALLOWSCRIPTS; retry uses a clean userconfig without changing pins. Full npm/Bun release gates will run only in CI."
  "2026-10-21T21:48:09.122Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6u9Nrl and same-class self-review findings: temporarily restored only repairSchedule from the pre-review head, keeping all new regressions and other functions intact. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"post-horizon|deadline placement|late deadlines\" test/deadline-repair.test.ts failed 0/3 (exit 1), all with false no_allowed_repair. Restored source immediately; same command passed 3/3 (exit 0). pm test pm-gantt-chart-deadline-repair --run --progress passed both linked commands: repair/scheduler/smoke 94/94 and focused regressions 3/3, no failures/skips/cancellations or timeouts. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint and npm run build passed; dist rebuilt. Latest full-PR self-review found no further instances beyond deadline placement in the shared repairSchedule baseline/candidate path. No thresholds or dependency pins changed. Evidence: docs/deadline-repair-validation.md. CI full release gates pending push."
  "2026-10-21T21:53:44.972Z",codex-agent,"Verified review code commit 38ed6e9a9a146d8f919e96ac2f07a56cc023673b: CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/actions/runs/39681761078 completed successfully. Node 26 npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 284/284 tests, 0 failures/skips/cancellations, 100.00% lines/branches/functions across 3 runtime source files, 0% duplication, 0 production audit vulnerabilities. Node 22.18.0 passed 284/284 at the same coverage thresholds. Strict PM health, committed dist consistency, packed acceptance for npm/current, Bun/current and npm/minimum host, changelog and workflow contracts passed. Local linked checks passed 94/94 and focused regressions 3/3; behavioral function revert failed 0/3 and restoration passed 3/3. No local timeouts occurred. PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6u9Nrl and the same-class dependency cases are fixed; latest review had no outside-diff/nitpick findings. No threads replied to/resolved, no mentions, merge or release. No PM CLI/SDK defect encountered; initial npm installation needed a clean userconfig and gh pr edit needed a REST fallback for a deprecated Projects field. Leave item in progress and release claim for orchestrator verification; subsequent handoff commit changes only PM evidence."
  "2026-10-22T09:38:03.679Z",pi-agent,"Review round for PR 164: remote head matches origin and is not behind main. Two unresolved threads remain, both on the deadline-repair tests. PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6vAaV0 is valid: the independent finish check compares UTC ISO day text, which false-passes the next local midnight on a positive offset and year-10000 overflow. PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6vAaV4 is valid: the harness loop accepts any refusal and does not prove camelCase limit aliases. Latest CodeRabbit review body has no outside-diff findings. Will fix both with regressions that fail on behavioural revert, then self-review the same classes."
  "2026-10-22T09:54:21.857Z",pi-agent,"PR 164 review fixes are test-only. PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6vAaV0: independent finish checks now compare each inclusive end with the next local midnight. Reverting only finishesByHorizon to ISO day text made node --test --test-name-pattern='horizon comparison' test/deadline-repair.test.ts fail 0/1 exit 1 (next local midnight compared true). Restored comparison passed 1/1. PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6vAaV4: harness cases now require ok plus one move, or invalid_scenario and exit 2. Zero kebab-case and camelCase limits are included because a positive capacity offer alone hides ignored aliases. Deferring the dependent while forbidding the prerequisite is ok, not no_allowed_repair. Dropping only camelCase keys from deadlineRepairOptions made node --test --test-name-pattern='real no-git tracker' test/deadline-repair.test.ts fail 0/1 exit 1 (camelCase maxChanges 0 ignored, capacity repair returned ok). Aliases restored to the implementation that had passed 1/1. Latest CodeRabbit review had no outside-diff findings. Self-review found no other UTC day-text ordering check in the repair path."
  "2026-10-22T10:10:45.744Z",codex-agent,"Continuation audit: remote PR 164 head pulled with no unpublished commits; origin/main is an ancestor. Read all comments on both unresolved threads and latest CodeRabbit review; no outside-diff findings. Retained the draft after review; production option aliases are intact. Strengthened the date regression to run explicitly under UTC and Europe/Vienna with timezone restoration. Self-review isolated malformed capacity using valid dates and added an explicit no_allowed_repair harness case. Independently repeating behavioral revert proofs, then full npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-22T10:14:19.876Z",codex-agent,"Independently verified date-oracle revert proof: replacing only finishesByHorizon with UTC ISO day string comparison made node --test --test-name-pattern=\"horizon comparison\" test/deadline-repair.test.ts fail 0/1 (exit 1, true instead of false). Restoring only that helper passed 1/1, exit 0. The regression explicitly covers UTC, Europe/Vienna and year overflow. No broken mutation remains. Installation and the real no-git harness are still running under heavy host load."
  "2026-10-22T10:27:02.549Z",codex-agent,"Independent behavioral proofs completed. Date helper revert failed 0/1 and restoration passed 1/1. Removing only camelCase lookup in deadlineRepairOptions failed the real no-git tracker test 0/1 (exit 1, ignored maxChanges zero returned ok). Restored it, then removing only malformed-capacity suffix rejection failed the same test 0/1 (exit 1, invalid capacity returned ok). Production index.ts restored byte-for-byte to HEAD after both proofs. Expanded harness had passed 1/1 before mutations; build:test and lint passed. CI-provisioned isolated strict PM health passed with required merge drivers and no history drift; only inherited stale-item and historical-provenance warnings remain. No dependency or threshold changes."
  "2026-10-22T10:43:49.213Z",codex-agent,"Code and regression evidence committed as fe9aeb6. Distribution rebuild is byte-identical. PM-linked checks passed: repair/scheduler/smoke 95/95, deadline-placement regressions 3/3, horizon regression 1/1, real no-git harness 1/1, all with zero failures/skips/cancellations. The initial linked broad and no-git runs hit the default 120-second execution timeout under host load; retries using --timeout 1200 passed in 422 and 147 seconds respectively. No assertions or release thresholds changed. Full isolated npm release gate is running; Bun follows after npm succeeds."
  "2026-10-22T11:04:27.654Z",codex-agent,"Final review gate evidence for code commit fe9aeb6: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed in full locally with isolated HOME and Git configuration. Each passed 285/285 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 100.00% lines/branches/functions across all 3 configured runtime sources, 0% duplication and 0 production vulnerabilities. Each passed npm-current, bun-current and npm-minimum packed scenarios, changelog/date/workflow/docstring/publish-attestation checks. Build output remains byte-identical. PM linked checks passed 95/95, 3/3, 1/1 and 1/1; only the initial default-120-second PM runner attempts timed out, and retries at 1200 seconds passed. All three behavioral revert proofs failed 0/1 with expected assertions; all source mutations were restored. Both unresolved threads are valid and addressed; latest CodeRabbit body has no outside-diff findings. Self-review additionally isolated malformed capacity validation and checked explicit forbidden-move refusal. No thread replies/resolutions, mentions, merge or release. No new PM CLI/SDK defect found. Leave item in progress for orchestrator verification; release ownership."
  "2026-10-23T15:25:57.344Z",codex-agent,"DELIVERED: merged PR #164 (24fe1f25d8fd275b0bfd74090d0044f16f2a6823) is an ancestor of audited main 9c887a56a99c7108591d9f223d09e3937ecf3e55. Inspected on main: test/deadline-repair.test.ts, docs/deadline-repair-validation.md. Minimal capacity/scope repairs use existing infeasible scheduling, preserve forbidden moves/prerequisites/horizons and honest exhausted-search refusals; no-git SDK/CLI/public-copy and full npm/Bun gates are retained. This tracker audit inspected existing tests/files; it does not claim a new full product test run."
